    "key_findings": [
      "Open information (OI) from web datasets exists and is strongly correlated with public information (PI).",
      "The uncorrelated component of open information provides information over and above public information, proving material significance for pricing models.",
      "Integrating open information into GARCH and VAR models yields statistically significant coefficients and improvements in in-sample fit and out-of-sample forecast accuracy."
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "The influence of open information is relatively feeble compared to volatility persistence.",
      "The impact varies depending on model selection and can be overridden by specific transformations such as in integrated-GARCH models.",
      "Diebold-Mariano tests for forecast accuracy improvements were statistically insignificant in most individual samples at the 10% level."
    ],
